---
// Figure: how many rebuilds XFetch starts per expiry, and how early.
import SimFigure from '../shared/SimFigure.astro';
import Slider from '../shared/Slider.astro';
import Choice from '../shared/Choice.astro';
import Readout from '../shared/Readout.astro';
import './stampedes.css';
interface Props { number: number }
const { number } = Astro.props;
---
<SimFigure number={number} id="st-xfetch-size" title="β sets the duplicates; traffic sets the head start" controls="none"
  caption="Simulation of the XFetch rule for one key with Poisson arrivals: 20,000 expiries for each value of β, nothing else coordinating the rebuilds, sampled exactly from the Poisson model of arrivals (a request-by-request simulation gives the same values). A rebuild time is how long one rebuild takes (200 ms in the article's example, so 500 requests a second is 100 requests per rebuild time). The solid line is the derived e to the power 1/β. The dotted brown line is the paper's Theorem 7 expression at each β, (e to the 1/β − 1)(β + 1/e), which the paper states as an upper bound and which gives e − 1/e ≈ 2.35 at β = 1.">
  <Slider slot="params" name="beta" label="β" min={0.5} max={3} step={0.25} value={1} />
  <Choice slot="params" name="rate" label="Requests per rebuild time" value="100"
    options={[{ value: '10', label: '10' }, { value: '100', label: '100' }, { value: '1000', label: '1,000' }, { value: '10000', label: '10,000' }]} />
  <Fragment slot="stats">
    <Readout name="size" label="Rebuilds per expiry, simulated" kind="database" />
    <Readout name="derived" label="Derived, e to the 1/β" kind="neutral" />
    <Readout name="lead" label="First rebuild, rebuild times before expiry (formula)" kind="neutral" />
    <Readout name="late" label="Expiries reached before the rebuild finished" kind="neutral" />
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="text">
    <p>The chart plots the average number of rebuilds per expiry against β. The simulated points sit on the derived line, e to the power 1/β: about 7.4 at β = 0.5, 2.7 at β = 1, 1.6 at β = 2 and 1.4 at β = 3. Changing the traffic from 100 to 10,000 requests per rebuild time leaves them where they are. It moves only the head start: at β = 1 the first rebuild starts on average about 5.2 rebuild times before expiry with 100 requests per rebuild time and about 9.8 with 10,000. With only 10 requests per rebuild time and β = 0.5, about half the expiries pass before the first rebuild finishes, and the count falls below the line because rebuilds started after the expiry follow the plain miss rate. The dotted line, the paper's Theorem 7 expression, gives e − 1/e ≈ 2.35 at β = 1 and lies below the simulated values at every β.</p>
  </Fragment>
</SimFigure>
<script>
  import { bindParams, setReadouts } from '../shared/player.mjs';
  import { lineChart } from '../shared/chart.mjs';
  import { seededRandom } from '../shared/sim.mjs';
  import { summarise, expectedSize, expectedLead, paperBound } from './xfetch-model.mjs';

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-figure-id="st-xfetch-size"]').forEach(root => {
    const BETAS = Array.from({ length: 21 }, (_, i) => 0.5 + i * 0.125);
    const chart = lineChart(root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-scene]')!, {
      label: 'Average rebuilds per expiry against β: simulated, e to the power 1 over β, and the paper’s Theorem 7 bound',
      height: 240,
      x: { label: 'β', domain: [0.5, 3], format: (v: number) => String(v) },
      y: { label: 'Rebuilds per expiry', domain: [0, 8] },
      series: [
        { id: 'derived', label: 'Derived, e to the 1/β', kind: 'neutral', dash: '' },
        { id: 'sim', label: 'Simulated', kind: 'database', dash: '6 4' },
        { id: 'paper', label: 'Paper’s Theorem 7 bound', kind: 'expiry', dash: '2 3' },
      ],
    });
    const curve = (f: (b: number) => number) => Array.from({ length: 101 }, (_, i) => { const b = 0.5 + i * 0.025; return [b, f(b)]; });
    chart.set('derived', curve(expectedSize));
    chart.set('paper', curve(paperBound));
    const cache = new Map<string, any>();
    const summary = (rate: number, beta: number) => {
      const key = `${rate}:${beta}`;
      if (!cache.has(key)) cache.set(key, summarise(seededRandom(11), { rate, beta, cycles: 20000 }));
      return cache.get(key);
    };
    bindParams(root, params => {
      const rate = Number(params.rate), beta = params.beta;
      chart.set('sim', BETAS.map(b => [b, summary(rate, b).size]));
      chart.render();
      chart.mark('now', beta, `β = ${beta}`, 'neutral');
      const s = summary(rate, beta);
      setReadouts(root, {
        size: s.size.toFixed(2),
        derived: expectedSize(beta).toFixed(2),
        lead: `${s.lead.toFixed(1)} (${expectedLead(rate, beta).toFixed(1)})`,
        late: `${Math.round(s.lateShare * 100)}%`,
      });
    });
  });
</script>
